Tim Starr: 
> I think a transhuman would have the same purpose of
> extending and enhancing his life as I would.  However, I do think that
> the tactics by which this strategy would be pursued would be greatly
> different for transhumans, including tactics which would be harmful to
> remaining mehums or just plain unintelligible to them.

In particular, I suspect transhumans will have a quite sophisticated
understanding of humans.  They'll understand humans better than
humans themselves.  They'll be able to "put themselves in the
shoes" of humans, "simulating" their responses in various
competitive situations.  In contrast, they'll have as many
misunderstandings betweeen similarly capable transhumans as
humans have between each other.  Perhaps more, as the intellectual
diversity of transhumans is likely to be greater.

As time goes on and humans become less important, empathy with
humans will become a proportionately more minor skill, although
in absolute terms it will still be around as long as humans
are around.

